- AutoDebug investigated apparent output_gate_type=swish / HF sigmoid discrepancy. Initial child sandbox preflight failed because unprivileged namespaces are unavailable; retried with explicitly authorized AUTODEBUG_SKIP_CHILD_SANDBOX=1. AUTODEBUG.md resolves this as separate linear and full attention gates; no patch needed.
- Initial functional_decoder.py and real-weight run_decoder.py are unvalidated. No performance or accuracy claims yet. No local checkpoint commit until clean-pass review.

## First functional results and remediation

Hardware command environment: `docker exec -e USER=mvasiljev -e TT_METAL_HOME=/workspace -e TT_METAL_CACHE=/workspace/.cache/tt-metal-cache -e PYTHONPATH=/workspace -e TT_METAL_TRACE_ALLOC_TRACKING=1 -e TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR=/workspace/.cache/torchinductor qwen38-functional-build bash -lc '<command>'`.
Runner command: `python -m models.autoports.qwen_qwen3_8_27b.tests.run_decoder --layer <0|3> --seq <N> [--batch B] [--resume] --output <artifact.json>`.

- Mesh smoke passed after correcting `device_ids` to `physical_device_ids` and setting writable TT_METAL_CACHE. Actual grid 11x10. Runtime uses `WormholeComputeKernelConfig` on Blackhole in this checkout (no separate BlackholeComputeKernelConfig symbol).
- Real-weight smoke32: linear prefill/decode PCC .999957/.999979; full .999830/.999837. Three identical trace replays were bitwise identical, tracking enabled.
- Real-weight 129-token full attention: prefill .999836, decode .999873, changed-input/position decode .999893, resume at128 PCC1.0.
- Batch32 linear failed fused recurrence's BH<=110 assertion (1536 heads). Split only recurrence batches into at most2 requests. Retest (`linear_b32_129_resume_fixed.json`) passed prefill .999794, decode .999652, changed-input .999315, resume1.0. This is a kernel scheduling limit, not an accepted batch-capability reduction.
- Batch32 full attention passed all analogous checks (`full_b32_129_resume.json`).
- Linear16385 failed: prefill .992926, decode .990660. Diagnostic recurrent-state PCC .907568 versus convolution history .999992 (`long_linear_debug/baseline_states.log`). BF16 L2 parity experiment failed to repair it (`bf16_l2.log`) and was reverted.
- CPU reference schedule control passed last mixer .999998 and state .999984 (`hf_schedule_control_fixed.log`), excluding reference chunk boundaries as the major divergence. Initial control script compared wrong shapes; that failure is preserved in hf_schedule_control.log and is not evidence.
- AutoDebug/AutoFix recurrence investigation is active. Static source shows fused recurrence missing FP32 unpack-to-destination and using FPU state decay/subtraction. Decoder-local generic-op workaround is under device validation, not yet a verified repair.
- Full16385 passed prefill .999955, decode .999833, changed-input .999893. Scalar chunk offsets compiled separate SDPA programs. Device tensor chunk offsets preserve those results (`full_16385_tensor_aligned.json`) and permit reuse. Flexible SDPA requires page-table rows multiple32 bytes; physical page capacity is rounded to eight32-token pages without restricting logical lengths. First tensor-offset probe failed this exact alignment requirement and is preserved (`full_16385_tensor_offset.log`).
- Full advertised-context prefill command now running: `--layer 3 --seq 262144 --prefill-only`, artifacts full_262144.*. Long reference checks final128 outputs against the full prefix cache; TT computes every logical output. This is subset output comparison, not reduced context.
- Full262144 prefill completed with real weights and PCC .996442795 on the final128 outputs using all262144 tokens of prefix state (`full_262144.json`). No context reduction. Next run tests262142 non-aligned prefill then decode at positions262142 and262143.

