    25	/*
    26	 * _float_to_int32_positive_ use branch to handle special cases
    27	 * With exp21f function, some of these cases never happen (e.g. negative exponent, overflow)
    28	 * This allow for a branch free (and much smaller algorithm) to compute integer value
    29	 *
    30	 * The constraint on `val` is: 0 <= val < 128.0f
    31	 * Note: Unlike _float_to_int32_positive, this function assumes that
    32	 * value has been been divided by 2^23. Output value will be scaled by 2^23 compared to 'val'.
    33	 * If that was not the case, we would have had to shift by `exp - 23` instead of `exp`
    34	 * This saves 1 SFPADDI instruction.
