    44	/*
    45	 * Unsafe core of BF16 21f exp: skips the xlog2 clamp present in
    46	 * _sfpu_exp_21f_bf16_. The caller MUST ensure `val * (1/ln2) + 127`
    47	 * stays in [0, 256) (roughly val ∈ [-88.0, 88.7]) — otherwise the
    48	 * implicit float→int conversion in _float_to_int32_for_exp_21f_ can
    49	 * wrap and produce garbage.
    50	 *
    51	 * Use this variant when the caller has already clamped its input (e.g. i1's
    52	 * asymptotic path operates on |x| ∈ [10, 88.5]).
