    55	 * (e.g. logaddexp): it can load the fractional-part coefficients once, before its loop.
    56	 * Each is a full fp32 value, two SFPLOADIs, which the one-argument form reloads on every
    57	 * call. Pass EXP_21F_BF16_C0..C2, each as a float or as a vFloat already holding it: like
    58	 * PolynomialEvaluator::eval, the overload takes either, so the one-argument form, which
    59	 * passes floats, compiles exactly as it did before.
