The source audit supports a leading precision hypothesis, but it does not prove the cause of the reported PCC values. A small host-only calculation shows that repeated BF16 sum updates can lose most contributions at this chunk count. I’ll make the first proposed check a single-input comparison with larger decode chunks, followed by an attention-only comparison using identical Q/K/V tensors. Both separate this hypothesis from model and cache differences.

